From 18fa02696d2465bd4db4857ee54c323f94f28f48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cpkt9762 <cpkt9762@163.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 16:37:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(search): fall back to any-term matches when a default
 search finds nothing

When match_mode is omitted or blank and an all-term search finds nothing for
two or more distinct searchable terms, MCP mem_search, HTTP /search and the
CLI rerun the query as an any-term LIKE search ranked by matched term count.
They mark the results explicitly: an explanation line and [k/N] per result
in text output, plus matched_terms, match_fallback and
X-Engram-Search-Fallback in structured output.

Explicit all or any, single-term and term-less queries, and all-term hits
are unchanged, and so are internal store callers such as conflict candidates.
A blank mode counts as omitted because models often fill optional strings
with "". Pi and DSH pass the new fields through to the model unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Codex (gpt-6.1-sol) <noreply@openai.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
